{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CopilotKit/CopilotKit/pulls/3433","id":3392370510,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJxJfAc7KM3dO","html_url":"https://github.com/CopilotKit/CopilotKit/pull/3433","diff_url":"https://github.com/CopilotKit/CopilotKit/pull/3433.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/CopilotKit/CopilotKit/pull/3433.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CopilotKit/CopilotKit/issues/3433","number":3433,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"fix: detect default provider message IDs to prevent collisions","user":{"login":"giulio-leone","id":6887247,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4ODcyNDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6887247?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/giulio-leone","html_url":"https://github.com/giulio-leone","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giulio-leone/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giulio-leone/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giulio-leone/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giulio-leone/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giulio-leone/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giulio-leone/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giulio-leone/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giulio-leone/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giulio-leone/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nFixes #3410\n\n`@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` (and similar providers) emit default/placeholder message IDs like `txt-0`, `reasoning-0`, `txt-1`, etc. These are sequential content-block indices that **reset for every response**, not unique message identifiers.\n\nThe existing check only filtered the literal `\"0\"`:\n```ts\nif (providedId && providedId !== \"0\") {\n  // used as messageId\n}\n```\n\nThis let pattern-based defaults like `\"txt-0\"` and `\"reasoning-0\"` pass through, causing **all messages across responses to share the same ID**. The frontend then merges/overwrites messages that should be separate.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` provider generates IDs using a `<type>-<index>` pattern (e.g., `txt-0`, `txt-1`, `reasoning-0`) as internal content block indices. These are not meant to be globally unique — they reset for each new response. When CopilotKit treats them as real message IDs, separate messages get the same ID.\n\n## Fix\n\nReplace the equality check with a regex pattern that detects known default ID formats:\n\n```ts\nconst DEFAULT_PROVIDER_ID_PATTERN = /^(?:\\d+|(?:txt|reasoning)-\\d+)$/;\n\n// Before: providedId !== \"0\"\n// After:  !DEFAULT_PROVIDER_ID_PATTERN.test(providedId)\n```\n\nThis catches:\n- Pure numeric IDs: `\"0\"`, `\"1\"`, `\"2\"`, ...\n- Text block indices: `\"txt-0\"`, `\"txt-1\"`, ...\n- Reasoning block indices: `\"reasoning-0\"`, `\"reasoning-1\"`, ...\n\nGenuine provider IDs (e.g., `\"msg_abc123\"`, UUIDs, `\"chatcmpl-xyz\"`) are unaffected.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`packages/v2/agent/src/index.ts`**: Added `DEFAULT_PROVIDER_ID_PATTERN` regex constant; updated `reasoning-start` and `text-start` handlers to use pattern matching instead of equality check\n- **`packages/v2/agent/src/__tests__/basic-agent.test.ts`**: Added regression tests for `\"txt-0\"` and `\"reasoning-0\"` default IDs\n\n## Testing\n\nAll 141 existing tests pass, plus 2 new regression tests:\n- `should generate unique messageId when provider returns default pattern IDs like 'txt-0'`\n- `should generate unique reasoningMessageId when provider returns 'reasoning-0'`\n","created_at":"2026-03-12T23:38:30Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:41:45Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"mme","id":247775,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0Nzc3NQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247775?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users